Package: RiemannFinMath
Type: Package
Title: Bond, Curve, Option, Credit and Rate Model Calculations from a Rust Library
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Eiichi", "Horigome", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "besuke.poripori@gmail.com"),
    person("The QuantLib authors", role = "cph", comment = "Rust code derived from QuantLib; see inst/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES"),
    person("The authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = "cph", comment = "Bundled in src/rust/vendor.tar.xz of a source package"))
Description: R entry point of the RiemannFinMath financial library. The calculations are
    in Rust; the R functions convert dates and return tibbles. Dates, calendars and
    conventions follow QuantLib, and everything is passed explicitly. Sensitivities come
    from automatic differentiation.
